        <div class="jcBand">
            <div id="pnlJobDescription">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <div style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;"><strong>Cal OES is recruiting for Limited Term positions and Emergency Hire Appointments in support of the Disaster Response and Recovery efforts in Southern California.</strong></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong style="text-decoration-line: underline;">Job Summary:</strong></span><br /></span><div>Under the general direction of the Infrastructure Services unit, IT Manager I, the IT Specialist II will provide support for the highly complex user and device connectivity and data services tasks. These tasks will include but are not limited to the design, implementation, and maintenance of a switching and routing environment supporting the California Office of Emergency Services (Cal OES). This will include the monitoring of network traffic and events. Cal OES utilizes a combination of terrestrial commercial data circuits, leased satellite bandwidth, microwave, and commercial mobility solutions to maintain data connectivity throughout the State. This position works independently at times with little or no direct supervision and acts as a lead to other staff and as a member of diverse project teams. This position provides data services critical to the security and success of Cal OES to meet its operational mission.</div><div><br /></div><div>This position will deal with California Law Enforcement Telecommunication System (CLETS) and DHS/ FEMA Secure information and services, as such; a background check via Live Scan and possible need for secret security clearance will be required to fulfill the responsibilities of this position.</div><div><br /></div><div>This position will require travel to other locations to perform system maintenance and deployments.</div></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br /></span></div><div style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><strong>** Limited Term positions may be appointed up to 12 months or extended to 24 months with the possibility of becoming permanent.**</strong> </span></div><div><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">For Limited Term positions please review the benefit information on the CalHR website and the CalPERS website.</span></li></ul><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> </span></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 12pt;">**Emergency Appointment (Ehire) will be considered**</span></strong></div><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">An emergency hire appointment can work up to 189 days in 12 consecutive months, based on the needs of the disaster.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Positions are paid on an hourly basis, once a month, during the first week of the month following the closure of the pay period. An emergency hire appointment is not eligible for medical benefits or a retirement program.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Emergency hire appointments earn state service and sick leave and vacation based upon actual time worked.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Civil Service Examinations are <strong>not</strong> required for appointment.</span></li></ul><div><div>**Applications are scheduled to be released to the hiring manager on the following dates:</div><ul><li>February 12, 2025</li><li>February 19, 2025</li><li>February 26, 2025</li></ul></div><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=26387369&name=19-20527-1414-904Combined.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
                </p>
            
</div>

            <div id="pnlWorkingConditions">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Working Conditions</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <div><strong>This position is Headquartered and reports to the office located at Mather, CA.<br /><br /></strong>Must be willing to be deployed at an unknown location for possibly weeks at a time.<br /></div>
                </p>
            
</div>
